</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:173%;">Appendix</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Organisation of Appendix</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The rest of the appendix is organized as follows.
In <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Independence Stability ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>,
we justify Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.1 Contextual Independence ‣ 3 Method ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> by demonstrating that it holds
for Transformer-based masked language models,
which is a direct consequence of the Transformer’s attention mechanism.
In <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Implementation and Experiments ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>, we provide additional experimental details and results.
In <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Masked Diffusion Models for Proteins ‣ Appendix C Implementation and Experiments ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, we provide some preliminary experiments on a protein masked diffusion model.
In <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Denoising Process ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>, we provide two examples of text that is generated by PUNT.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Remark on Notation:</em>
In addition to standard notation as defined in the paper,
in the appendix, we will also use upper-case bold letters (such as <span id="A1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">A</span>) to denote tensors.
We will use lowercase and unbolded letters to denote scalars (such as <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>).
In addition, we may have uppercase letters (such as <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V</annotation></semantics></math>) annotations to help annotate different matrices.
This is to accommodate standard notation used in the literature.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Independence Stability</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we demonstrate that Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.1 Contextual Independence ‣ 3 Method ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>
holds for Transformer-based masked language models,
which is a direct consequence of the Transformer’s attention mechanism.
Let us start with recalling the assumption.
See <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.1 Contextual Independence ‣ 3 Method ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>
Next, we recall the design of attention mechanism and discuss prior works</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Attention-Based Independence.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In transformers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al., (2023)</a></cite>,
the attention weights control information flow between positions.
For an input sequence <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}=(\mathbf{X}^{1},\ldots,\mathbf{X}^{L})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}=(\mathbf{X}^{1},\ldots,\mathbf{X}^{L})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{in}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
each attention head computes query, key, and value vectors for every position:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}^{i}=\mathbf{W}^{Q}\mathbf{X}^{i},\quad\mathbf{K}^{i}=\mathbf{W}^{K}\mathbf{X}^{i},\quad\mathbf{V}^{i}=\mathbf{W}^{V}\mathbf{X}^{i}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}^{i}=\mathbf{W}^{Q}\mathbf{X}^{i},\quad\mathbf{K}^{i}=\mathbf{W}^{K}\mathbf{X}^{i},\quad\mathbf{V}^{i}=\mathbf{W}^{V}\mathbf{X}^{i},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{Q},\mathbf{W}^{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times d_{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{Q},\mathbf{W}^{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{k}\times d_{in}}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times d_{in}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>V</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{v}\times d_{in}}</annotation></semantics></math> are learned weight matrices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The attention mechanism then computes pairwise attention scores between
all positions through scaled dot products:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}=\mathrm{softmax}\!\left(\frac{\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.720em;" width="3.720em"><mi>softmax</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}=\mathrm{softmax}\!\left(\frac{\mathbf{Q}\mathbf{K}^{\top}}{\sqrt{d_{k}}}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q},\mathbf{K}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> stack the query and key vectors across all positions.
The attention weights <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> quantify how much position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> influences position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>,
computed via normalized dot-product similarity.
The output of one head combines value vectors weighted by these attention scores:
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{head}_{h}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{v}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐡𝐞𝐚𝐝</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐀𝐕</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{head}_{h}=\mathbf{A}\mathbf{V}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{v}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Finally, outputs of different heads are stacked to get,
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z_{i}}=\textrm{concat}{\left(\mathbf{head}^{i}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{head}^{i}_{H}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡𝐞𝐚𝐝</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐡𝐞𝐚𝐝</mi><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z_{i}}=\textrm{concat}{\left(\mathbf{head}^{i}_{1},\ldots,\mathbf{head}^{i}_{H}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math>
The output of the layer <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}=(\mathbf{Y}^{1},\ldots,\mathbf{Y}^{L})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{out}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}=(\mathbf{Y}^{1},\ldots,\mathbf{Y}^{L})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d_{out}}</annotation></semantics></math>
is calculated as <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}^{i}=F(\mathbf{Z}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}^{i}=F(\mathbf{Z}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>
by application to each of the coordinates of MLP together
with normalization layers and skip connections.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, the attention weights <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> directly control information flow:
when <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{ij}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{ij}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>’s value vector
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> contributes nothing to position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s output.
The model’s final predictions are obtained by applying softmax to the last layer’s output:
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M}):=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{Y}^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M}):=\mathrm{softmax}(\mathbf{Y}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})=p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{y}^{R},\mathbf{x}^{-M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})=p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{y}^{R},\mathbf{x}^{-M})</annotation></semantics></math>
holds if and only if <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> remains unchanged when tokens at positions <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> are revealed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stability of Unmasked Tokens.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., (2025)</a></cite>
have demonstrated that during iterative inference,
the query, key, and value vectors (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>)
for already unmasked tokens, remain stable and can be cached for computational efficiency.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.21961v1/Figures/kl_errors_vs_attention.png" id="A2.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/114;" width="476" height="114" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A2.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Joint distribution of <math id="A2.F6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\operatorname{KL}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\operatorname{KL}}</annotation></semantics></math> – the sampling error and <math id="A2.F6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> – the total attention to the previous tokens revealed in parallel.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Why Independence Stability Holds.</h5>

<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.21961v1/Figures/hist_attention_stats.png" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/166;" width="476" height="166" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A2.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Difference between attention statistics for
<math id="A2.F7.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M},\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M},\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}})</annotation></semantics></math>
relative to the same statistics computed while evaluating <math id="A2.F7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})</annotation></semantics></math>.
</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let us return to Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.1 Contextual Independence ‣ 3 Method ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. First, we discuss padding end-of-sequence (EOS) tokens, which are used to fill the unused suffix reserved for an answer. By design, if there is an EOS token in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math> to the left of position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{i}(\text{EOS}|x^{-M})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>EOS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{i}(\text{EOS}|x^{-M})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and the assumption automatically holds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For regular tokens, we note that the stability property implies that in both cases, when we condition on <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{y}^{U},\mathbf{x}^{-M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>U</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{y}^{U},\mathbf{x}^{-M})</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{x}^{-M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{x}^{-M})</annotation></semantics></math>, the representations (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>) stay the same, while the main change happens for tokens in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The stability property allows us to concentrate on the information flow between position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and tentatively unmasked subset <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>U</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we recall governed by attention weights vector <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{iU}:={\left(A_{i,u_{1}},\ldots,A_{i,u_{|U|}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{iU}:={\left(A_{i,u_{1}},\ldots,A_{i,u_{|U|}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we argue that a token <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is conditionally independent
of a set of tokens <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>U</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{U}</annotation></semantics></math> given the remaining tokens <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math>
if and only if the total attention from position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to all positions in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is negligible
across all layers and heads, or more formally, if <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{iU}\right\rVert_{1}=\sum_{u\in U}A_{iu}&lt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{iU}\right\rVert_{1}=\sum_{u\in U}A_{iu}&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for some small <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now consider any subset <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\subset U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\subset U</annotation></semantics></math>.
The non-negativity of attention weights (a direct consequence of the softmax operation)
yields the inequality:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{iW}\right\rVert_{1}=\sum_{w\in W}A_{iw}\leq\sum_{u\in U}A_{iu}=\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{iU}\right\rVert_{1}&lt;\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{iW}\right\rVert_{1}=\sum_{w\in W}A_{iw}\leq\sum_{u\in U}A_{iu}=\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{iU}\right\rVert_{1}&lt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This demonstrates that if position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> pays negligible attention to the entire set <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>,
it necessarily pays negligible attention to any subset <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\subset U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\subset U</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently, the conditional distribution at position <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> remains approximately invariant when
conditioning on tokens at positions in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>:
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{y}^{W},\mathbf{x}^{-M})\approx p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>W</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{y}^{W},\mathbf{x}^{-M})\approx p_{\theta}^{i}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This relationship directly corresponds to Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.1 Contextual Independence ‣ 3 Method ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> (Independence Stability).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Empirical Validation</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same setup as was used in <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 PUNT Sampler Error Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, as a source of prompts, we use the first round requests from MTBench, and sample the responses using the PUNT algorithm with different thresholds <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=\left\{0.01,0.04,0.16,0.64\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.64</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\left\{0.01,0.04,0.16,0.64\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a step of the PUNT sampler with threshold <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of tokens unmasked at this step, sorted according to the confidence, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{R}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of sampled candidates, and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{-M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{-M}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of already revealed tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">As we demonstrated at <a href="#S4.F3" title="In 4 Experiments ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> sampled tokens satisfy</p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{\operatorname{KL}}=D_{\mathrm{KL}}{\left(p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M},\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}})\,\big\|\,p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})\right)}&lt;\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\operatorname{KL}}=D_{\mathrm{KL}}{\left(p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M},\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}})\,\big\|\,p^{r_{i}}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})\right)}&lt;\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For each token <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the total attention from token <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to previously revealed tokens <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{&lt;i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{&lt;i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all heads of the last layer, i.e.</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{A}=\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{r_{i}R_{&lt;i}}\right\rVert_{1}=\sum_{j&lt;i}A_{r_{i}r_{j}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{A}=\left\lVert\mathbf{A}_{r_{i}R_{&lt;i}}\right\rVert_{1}=\sum_{j&lt;i}A_{r_{i}r_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and plot (<a href="#A2.F6" title="In Stability of Unmasked Tokens. ‣ Appendix B Independence Stability ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) the distribution of pairs (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{\operatorname{KL}},\delta_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{\operatorname{KL}},\delta_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>) for different thresholds.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We also compute the change of the layer output <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}^{r_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐘</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}^{r_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and how it changes when we condition on <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the normalized difference metric to compute the change, which is defined as
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{normalized\_difference}(a,b):=\left\lVert a-b\right\rVert_{2}/\left\lVert a\right\rVert_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>normalized</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>difference</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{normalized\_difference}(a,b):=\left\lVert a-b\right\rVert_{2}/\left\lVert a\right\rVert_{2},</annotation></semantics></math> and plot (<a href="#A2.F7" title="In Why Independence Stability Holds. ‣ Appendix B Independence Stability ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) the distribution of the change.
Finally, similar to unmasked tokens, we observed that representations <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}^{r_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐐</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}^{r_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}^{r_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐊</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}^{r_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{V}^{r_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐕</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{V}^{r_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> of masked token <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the attention layer also stays stable when we additionally condition on previously revealed tokens <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{R_{&lt;i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> PUNT (Parallel Unmasking with Non-influence Tests)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span>
masked sequence <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>,
vector of candidates <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>,
threshold <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span>
certified set <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\subseteq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\subseteq M</annotation></semantics></math> to unmask in parallel

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            Sort masked indices w.r.t. confidence heuristic <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> in decreasing order

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            Construct <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, the set of all masked indices.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leftarrow M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leftarrow M</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            Let <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{b}:=\{i\in[|M|]:\text{the }b\text{-th bit of }\text{bin}(i)=0\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>the </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>-th bit of </mtext><mtext>bin</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{b}:=\{i\in[|M|]:\text{the }b\text{-th bit of }\text{bin}(i)=0\}.</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\log|M|]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\log|M|]</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}\leftarrow R\cap B_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}\leftarrow R\cap B_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">(positions to tentatively unmask)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}\leftarrow R\setminus B_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}\leftarrow R\setminus B_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">(positions to check for dependence)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in S_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in S_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{j}\leftarrow\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(p^{j}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})\,\big\|\,p^{j}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M},\mathbf{y}^{S_{1}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}\leftarrow\mathrm{D}_{\mathrm{KL}}\big(p^{j}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M})\,\big\|\,p^{j}(\cdot\mid\mathbf{x}^{-M},\mathbf{y}^{S_{1}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}&gt;\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}&gt;\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
                 <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\leftarrow R\setminus\{j\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\leftarrow R\setminus\{j\}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Implementation and Experiments</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section evaluates the proposed planner PUNT (Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Empirical Validation ‣ Appendix B Independence Stability ‣ Parallel Sampling from Masked Diffusion Models via Conditional Independence Testing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>)
across diverse sequence generation tasks.
All experiments are conducted on A100 GPUs with 40GB memory.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">PUNT offers a clear win in step efficiency without compromising on quality.
However, this is not indicative of the underlying compute used, which is better captured by the number of forward passes (NFE).
In terms of NFE, it performs competitively, and particularly on long-sequence tasks,
it often surpasses the baselines.
We leave further per-step optimisation for future work.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate two state-of-the-art discrete diffusion models for natural language:
<span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLaDA-1.5</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025a, </a>)</cite> and <span id="A3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dream-v0-Instruct-7B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2025b, </a>)</cite>
(referred to as Llada and Dream, respectively). In this section, we detail the experimental setup,
including tasks, datasets, evaluation metrics, and baseline methods.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Tasks and Datasets</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assess PUNT’s performance on a variety of sequence generation tasks.
The evaluation relies on the following standard public datasets and their corresponding protocols:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Math word problems and formal math: GSM8K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al.,, 2021</a>)</cite>, MATH <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al.,, 2021</a>)</cite></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Code generation: HumanEval <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al.,, 2021</a>)</cite> and MBPP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Austin et al.,, 2021</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Instruction-following evaluation: IFEval <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al.,, 2023</a>)</cite></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Open-ended question benchmarks: MT-Bench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al.,, 2023</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Evaluation Metrics and Configuration</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use task-specific evaluation metrics and measure efficiency
in terms of the number of forward evaluations and the number of iterations PUNT takes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Quality Metrics:</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Math problems: Match accuracy (GSM8K)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Code generation: Pass@1 success rate (HumanEval, MBPP)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Instruction following: Strict/Loose prompt/instruction adherence (IFEval)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Open-ended generation: GPT-4o scoring 1-10 (MT-Bench)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.SSSx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Efficiency Metrics:</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Number of network function evaluations (NFE) per sequence</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Number of generation steps (PUNT-specific)</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A3.T1.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
